# SpaceFox listing description

SpaceFox is a space-themed watch face with a 24-hour clock, four configurable activity fields, and the next available launch with rocket artwork and a launch-site map. The countdown shows T- before a known launch time and T+ afterwards; reaching zero does not confirm liftoff. Rescheduled and stale information have separate indicators.

Choose from English, Russian, German, French and Spanish, configure the four fields and colors, and use the default public launch feed or a compatible feed of your own. Available activity readings depend on your watch. A connection through Garmin Connect is needed to update launch data; the last accepted data can remain available offline.

The ordinary 0.1.13 submission targets Forerunner 165 and 165 Music, Forerunner 965, Forerunner 170 and 170 Music, Forerunner 570 42mm, Forerunner 70, Venu 3S, Venu 4 41mm and vivoactive 6. The original card displays 0.1.13/Internal 8 PENDING in owner preview; public approval and physical delivery remain unobserved. The same signed package is published on GitHub. ACTIVE has second precision and four fields; LOW retains the full map contour/point, large clock/date/weekday, minute countdown and battery without four fields. The reddish reschedule override applies in both modes. Report issues at https://github.com/JekaMas/SpaceFox/issues. Privacy: https://github.com/JekaMas/SpaceFox/blob/main/docs/PRIVACY.md
